// Production pure-Pion full-station daemon (`whole_daemon.pion`), assembling `station_whole::WholeCore`
// onto `daemon_core.pion` with:
// - Pre-handover preparation (`on_init`): binds inherited `mcp_fd` (or `127.0.0.1:0`), serves `503` on
//   `/mcp` before readiness, NEVER opens SQLite primary writer before predecessor exit;
// - Atomic post-predecessor takeover (`on_predecessor_gone`): `WholeCore::open_after_predecessor_gone`
//   (`before_store` + `register_sqlite_js_lower` + SQLite open/migrate + handover snapshot restore +
//   live runner adoption reading native `"runner"` PID field + crash-recovery token adoption + active
//   job adoption) -> deletes snapshot ONLY after restore succeeds (never deletes on parse/restore error) ->
//   `ctx.mark_role_ready()`;
// - Production `stillfail/http/1` (`PEER_HTTP_ALPN`) station-to-station local port forward (HTTP/1.1
//   half-open streaming + `socket: true` WebSocket `101` proxy + `tcp: true`/`probe: true` + `ownPorts`
//   refusal incl. launcher `shown` port + write-completion-driven backpressure + serialized upstream writes +
//   late `tcp.open` cleanup);
// - Production `stillfail/admin/1` (`ALPN`) member AdminApi over `station_mesh::ServeEndpoint` with
//   Ed25519 JWT + revocation + workspace lock + personal lock (`onPersonalLock`) cryptographic verification
//   on stream 1 (exempt from generic 60s idle sweep), live revocation/lock kick on every cloud state update,
//   strict per-workspace Drive root isolation (`drive.workspaces[ws]`, never falling back to `$HOME`),
//   backpressured 64 KiB Drive download, Content-Length-verified Drive upload before atomic rename commit,
//   single-subscription SSE with `since`/`running`, and `OLDEST_CORE` floor on all routes;
// - Read-only `PeerIdentity::AuthenticatedStation` (`role: "viewer"`) on `PEER_ALPN`/`PEER_BYTES_ALPN`
//   (zero self-asserted identity headers);
// - Graceful `SIGUSR2` handover preserving running jobs & runners (`detach_all_for_handover`) with
//   error propagation on snapshot export/write failure vs full `SIGTERM`/`SIGINT` shutdown stopping jobs.

